@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+# Daily Grind account UI
+
+The site is static and has no authentication server or credential database. `/` and `/account/` display the account interface; `/home.html` preserves the original homepage. Without configuration, the UI uses a clearly marked preview account. Preview names and deletions persist in localStorage and never call WebAuthn APIs. Clear `daily-grind.preview-passkeys.v1` to reset the sample list. No real passkeys are registered in the preview.
+
+## Connect an authenticated backend
+
+Inject this configuration **before** the account module on both account HTML pages:
+
+```html
+<script>
+window.DAILY_GRIND_ACCOUNT = {
+  apiBase: '/api/account/passkeys',
+  csrfToken: 'SERVER_ISSUED_CSRF_TOKEN'
+};
+</script>
+```
+
+Use these same-origin endpoints:
+
+- `GET /api/account/passkeys`: list every credential belonging to the signed-in user.
+- `PUT /api/account/passkeys/:id`: persist the trimmed `{ "name": "My laptop" }` nickname, limited to 60 characters.
+- `DELETE /api/account/passkeys/:id`: delete that user's credential and return the complete remaining list in one transaction.
+
+Each successful endpoint returns the same complete, non-paginated JSON snapshot:
+
+```json
+{
+  "authenticated": true,
+  "complete": true,
+  "rpId": "coffee.example",
+  "user": { "id": "dXNlcg", "displayName": "Jamie Lee", "memberSince": 2024 },
+  "credentials": [
+    {
+      "id": "Y3JlZGVudGlhbA",
+      "name": "My laptop",
+      "provider": "iCloud Keychain",
+      "device": "laptop",
+      "current": true,
+      "registeredAt": 1779062400000,
+      "lastUsedAt": 1792713600000
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+`user.id` is the original WebAuthn user handle encoded as Base64URL. Credential IDs are also Base64URL strings. Dates are persisted epoch **milliseconds**, not formatted display strings. `current` means the credential used to establish the current session; it does not mean every device synced by that provider. Supported `device` hints are `laptop`, `phone`, `usb`, and `key`. Use verified registration metadata to supply friendly provider hints; unknown providers are safe to display generically.
+
+The server must validate the session, enforce ownership on every operation, validate nicknames, reject cross-origin mutations / verify CSRF tokens, and return 401/403 when authentication expires. Set `Cache-Control: no-store`. Never trust client-supplied user IDs. Enforce any recovery or recent-reauthentication policy on the backend before deletion. Failed live requests never fall back to preview data. The frontend warns when deleting the last credential; the server decides whether other recovery methods are sufficient.
+
+The client calls feature-detected `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials()` on initial authenticated load and after a successful delete. Only complete server-confirmed lists are signaled, including an empty list after the last deletion. It checks the RP domain and secure context. Browser support or provider failures don't undo a successful account deletion; the UI explains manual password-manager cleanup and offers retry on failure. Nickname changes don't call `signalCurrentUserDetails()`, since they do not rename the WebAuthn account user. The UI deliberately offers management only; registration requires a separate server-verified WebAuthn flow.
+
+## Code verification
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/passkey-service.test.mjs
+node --input-type=module --check < account.js
+node --check passkey-service.mjs
+```
+
+No dev/preview servers or browser verification are needed for these checks.
